## Why This Is Asked
This tests formulating a DP over partitions with a subarray-internal metric.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP
- Prefix sums
- Reconstruction pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
// DP skeleton
function maxValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i]+A[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const cut = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) {
     for (let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++) {
        let maxVal = -Infinity; let bestP = -1; let curMax = -Infinity;
        for (let p=i-1; p>=t-1; p--) {
           curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[p]);
           const val = dp[p][t-1] + (pref[i]-pref[p]) - curMax;
           if (val>maxVal) { maxVal=val; bestP=p; }
        }
        dp[i][t] = maxVal; cut[i][t] = bestP;
     }
  }
  return {value: dp[n][k], cuts: cut};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What is the time complexity and how would you optimize to O(nk) with a deque?
- How would you reconstruct the exact subarray endpoints?

## Why This Is Asked
Offers a new DP angle: path with exact turns, combining grid path DP with turn accounting. Tests deriving a tight state space, base cases, and reconstruction, mirroring routing-like constraints in real systems.

## Key Concepts
- Grid DP with an extra dimension for turns
- Two direction states to capture turns
- Reconstruction via backpointers
- Careful base/edge-case handling (start cell, negative infinities)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithTurns(grid, K) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  // 4D DP: [i][j][t][d]
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: m}, () =>
    Array.from({length: K+1}, () => [NEG, NEG])));
  dp[0][0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp[0][0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= K; t++) {
        if (i === 0 && j === 0) continue;
        // last move right
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][0] = Math.max(
            (dp[i][j-1][t][0] !== NEG ? dp[i][j-1][t][0] : NEG),
            (t > 0 && dp[i-1][j][t-1][1] !== NEG ? dp[i-1][j][t-1][1] : NEG)
          ) + grid[i][j];
        }
        // last move down
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][1] = Math.max(
            (dp[i-1][j][t][1] !== NEG ? dp[i-1][j][t][1] : NEG),
            (t > 0 && dp[i][j-1][t-1][0] !== NEG ? dp[i][j-1][t-1][0] : NEG)
          ) + grid[i][j];
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return Math.max(dp[n-1][m-1][K][0], dp[n-1][m-1][K][1]);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to allow at most k turns and also maximize path length if grid values included negative numbers?
- How would you optimize space to O(nmK) memory or better, and what would be the trade-offs for reconstruction?

